# 1. What are the four pillars of Object-Oriented Programming?

Encapsulation — Protecting data.  -> Access modifiers, methods
Abstraction — Hiding implementation details.  ->Interfaces, abstract classes
Inheritance — Reusing code from another class. ->extends
Polymorphism — One method or interface, different behaviors. -Overloading, overriding

